Beyond the 75 tasks: orchestrator.invoke() is wired end to end. The mode branch
was outstanding when the task list closed — every piece existed and nothing
joined them — so `invoke()` raised NotImplementedError. Both arms now run and
are tested offline: replay against a real fixture store, record through an
injected client.

Also beyond the 75 tasks, and closed rather than deferred: schema-validated
output now runs through invoke(). This file previously recorded it as not
implemented and handed it to E013's first real caller. That was wrong to leave —
validate_or_repair was unit-tested but unreachable from the entry point, so
TR-006 held in units and was violated on every call, and `repaired` and
validation-`failed` were unreachable on real rows. InvocationRequest gains an
optional output_schema; the failure path writes the row before raising (TR-008);
a repair in `replay` resolves a second fixture keyed on the instruction that
provoked it, so `repaired` is reachable in the mode CI runs. See qc-report.md,
"Closed since run 1", for the reasoning and what it cost.

Still not measured, recorded rather than implied: OBJ6 VC2, one live provider
invocation end to end. It needs a real credential and spends money. The smoke
check covers the gate, the credential handle and the guard exemption, and skips
the call itself — those are the 5 skips above. No automated run can discharge
it, by design.
